tle><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136212341.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[David Anthony Sanchez has been sentenced to 47 months in prison for defrauding a meme coin project out of $260,000 in cryptocurrency by mimicking streamer N3on's voice using artificial intelligence. He set up deceptive accounts posing as N3on and convinced project organizers to transfer cryptocurrency, all while utilizing AI-generated voice recordings that seemed authentic.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-man-sentenced-to-47-months-in-prison-for-using-ai-to-clone-streamer-n3ons-voice-and-steal-260000-in-cryptocurrency-from-a-meme-coin-project/articleshow/136212341.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-man-sentenced-to-47-months-in-prison-for-using-ai-to-clone-streamer-n3ons-voice-and-steal-260000-in-cryptocurrency-from-a-meme-coin-project/articleshow/136212341.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T15:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136212516,imgsize-1505509.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Anonymous California donors protect 120 acres of redwood forest for salmon]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136221249.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-anonymous-california-landowners-donated-conservation-rights-worth-680000-to-protect-120-acres-of-redwood-forest-and-endangered-salmon-habitat/articleshow/136221249.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-anonymous-california-landowners-donated-conservation-rights-worth-680000-to-protect-120-acres-of-redwood-forest-and-endangered-salmon-habitat/articleshow/136221249.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T17:29:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136221345,imgsize-2356034.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK developer misses nine-month deadline and forfeits £245,000 property deposit]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136220589.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-uk-developer-planned-to-build-32-homes-on-a-2-45-million-site-but-missed-a-nine-month-planning-deadline-the-high-court-has-now-allowed-the-seller-to-keep-its-245000-deposit/articleshow/136220589.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-uk-developer-planned-to-build-32-homes-on-a-2-45-million-site-but-missed-a-nine-month-planning-deadline-the-high-court-has-now-allowed-the-seller-to-keep-its-245000-deposit/articleshow/136220589.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T17:14:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136220888,imgsize-1941205.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Victoria’s Young Australian of the Year: Ryan Brigham wins award; charity raises over $500,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136182007.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ryan Brigham founded the charity Health in Focus after facing serious health challenges and hospital stays. The initiative has mobilized over 800 young volunteers to improve healthcare access both locally and internationally. It has raised more than $500,000 to deliver health education and resources to underserved communities. Healthcare programs like mobile cardiac screening clinics target early detection of cardiovascular issues.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-27-year-old-from-melbourne-who-has-been-through-more-than-10-operations-started-a-health-charity-at-21-and-with-800-young-volunteers-and-500000-raised-he-is-now-victorias-young-australian-of-the-year/articleshow/136182007.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-27-year-old-from-melbourne-who-has-been-through-more-than-10-operations-started-a-health-charity-at-21-and-with-800-young-volunteers-and-500000-raised-he-is-now-victorias-young-australian-of-the-year/articleshow/136182007.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T17:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136182158,imgsize-1180002.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indiana man ordered to transfer ex-wife $35,000 from retirement fund and pay $2,500 in fees]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136184321.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a recent ruling, Indiana resident Russell Mangas faced contempt charges for not transferring $35,000 to his ex-wife, as originally agreed during their divorce settlement. He tried to argue that later agreements invalidated this obligation, but the court highlighted his original intentions and upheld the contempt ruling, including a $2,500 fee to cover his ex-wife's attorney costs, reinforcing the mandate for him to finalize the retirement fund transfer.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-man-agreed-to-give-his-former-wife-35000-from-his-retirement-fund-then-argued-a-later-divorce-agreement-wiped-out-the-promise-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-transfer-obligation-and-2500-fees/articleshow/136184321.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-man-agreed-to-give-his-former-wife-35000-from-his-retirement-fund-then-argued-a-later-divorce-agreement-wiped-out-the-promise-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-transfer-obligation-and-2500-fees/articleshow/136184321.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T17:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136184432,imgsize-1823848.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New York man walks 2,500 miles across US pushing a shopping cart for freedom]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136218622.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-york-man-leaves-behind-his-everyday-life-to-walk-2500-miles-across-the-us-pushing-a-shopping-cart-spends-nearly-five-months-on-the-road-seeking-freedom-from-a-monotonous-routine-and-a-fresh-perspective-on-life/articleshow/136218622.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-york-man-leaves-behind-his-everyday-life-to-walk-2500-miles-across-the-us-pushing-a-shopping-cart-spends-nearly-five-months-on-the-road-seeking-freedom-from-a-monotonous-routine-and-a-fresh-perspective-on-life/articleshow/136218622.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T16:34:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136219408,imgsize-1409900.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chris Preble rushed into a burning Nebraska camper in June and pulled Judy Erickson to safety, suffering serious burns himself; five months later, he has been selected for an honour at the Nebraska-Iowa football game]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136212089.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chris Preble, while spending time at Harlan County Lake, saved Judy Erickson from a burning camper. Erickson, trapped inside, suffered from smoke inhalation and burns after a cooking accident. Preble entered the flames without hesitation, rescuing her but sustaining serious burns himself. Following his recovery, he was honored as Nebraska's citizen hero at the 16th annual Heroes Game.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/heroic-rescue-chris-preble-saves-judy-erickson-from-burning-camper-receives-nebraska-honor-at-iowa-game/articleshow/136212089.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/heroic-rescue-chris-preble-saves-judy-erickson-from-burning-camper-receives-nebraska-honor-at-iowa-game/articleshow/136212089.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T18:07:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136212089,imgsize-44620.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida woman ordered to pay $5.54 million after transferring mother's money in online scam]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136185086.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Florida appellate court reaffirmed a crucial ruling against Kimberly Langston after she mismanaged her mother's finances, transferring nearly $1.85 million due to an online romance scam. The court determined that she neglected her duty to verify the scammer's identity. This case highlights the importance of fiduciary responsibility in protecting elderly family members' financial interests.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-woman-transferred-1-85-million-of-her-mothers-money-to-people-directed-by-an-online-scammer-posing-as-a-french-billionaire-her-brother-sued-and-a-court-upheld-a-5-54-million-judgment-against-her/articleshow/136185086.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-woman-transferred-1-85-million-of-her-mothers-money-to-people-directed-by-an-online-scammer-posing-as-a-french-billionaire-her-brother-sued-and-a-court-upheld-a-5-54-million-judgment-against-her/articleshow/136185086.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T16:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136185153,imgsize-1076257.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Royal Caribbean bans couple for life after $405 car cleaning dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136217773.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-longtime-cruise-passenger-sued-royal-caribbean-over-a-405-car-cleaning-bill-after-claiming-celebrity-staff-directed-him-to-an-open-parking-lot-the-cruise-line-subsequently-banned-him-and-his-wife-for-life/articleshow/136217773.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-longtime-cruise-passenger-sued-royal-caribbean-over-a-405-car-cleaning-bill-after-claiming-celebrity-staff-directed-him-to-an-open-parking-lot-the-cruise-line-subsequently-banned-him-and-his-wife-for-life/articleshow/136217773.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T15:46:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136217910,imgsize-1993766.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Infosys sees eightfold rise in US H-1B approvals as Texas prepares to change visa policy: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136217489.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/infosys-sees-eightfold-rise-in-us-h-1b-approvals-as-texas-prepares-to-change-visa-policy-report/articleshow/136217489.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/infosys-sees-eightfold-rise-in-us-h-1b-approvals-as-texas-prepares-to-change-visa-policy-report/articleshow/136217489.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T15:39:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136217779,imgsize-624675.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[GTA 6 beats Valorant, Elden Ring and Diablo 4 combined to become biggest streaming launch ever]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136217009.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[GTA 6 achieved a record-breaking launch on November 19, exceeding previous livestreaming watch time records. The game attracted 420 million hours of watch time during its first week online. Additionally, it reached 7.91 million concurrent viewers, surpassing popular titles such as Valorant and Elden Ring. Prominent streamers like TheBurntPeanut and IShowSpeed contributed significantly to the game's viewership success.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/gta-6-beats-valorant-elden-ring-and-diablo-4-combined-to-become-biggest-streaming-launch-ever/articleshow/136217009.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/gta-6-beats-valorant-elden-ring-and-diablo-4-combined-to-become-biggest-streaming-launch-ever/articleshow/136217009.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T15:12:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136217090,imgsize-1034130.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian family gets A$1.55 million after rejecting insurer's A$1,000 goodwill offer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136212447.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Australian insurer, Hollard, has been fined A$2 million for delays in handling a family's storm-damage claim. The family rejected a A$1,000 goodwill offer as its home deteriorated and eventually received A$1.55 million after more than three years. The case comes amid wider scrutiny of insurance claim-handling failures in Australia.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-family-rejected-an-insurers-a1000-goodwill-offer-as-their-storm-damaged-home-deteriorated-hollard-eventually-paid-a1-55-million-and-a-court-later-imposed-a-separate-a2-million-penalty/articleshow/136212447.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-family-rejected-an-insurers-a1000-goodwill-offer-as-their-storm-damaged-home-deteriorated-hollard-eventually-paid-a1-55-million-and-a-court-later-imposed-a-separate-a2-million-penalty/articleshow/136212447.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-27T15:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136212991,imgsize-160978.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Hafiz-e-Quran’: LeT, JeM figures back Asim Munir as Pak army pushes to mainstream terror outfits]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136215131.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]